   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Merrow's towns once set clocks by the sun, which was a wiser and more natural system. The railway company forced its own time on the province, and residents lost something valuable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Merrow's towns set clocks by the sun until a Fenwick newspaper proposed a shared time. The assembly agreed at once, and the railway then adjusted its schedules.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"Merrow's towns once set clocks by the sun. Railway schedules made this confusing and unsafe, so the company used one standard time, which spread despite objections and later became law.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Merrow Line stopped in a dozen towns, and its timetables were hard to read. Passengers missed connections, and trains waiting on single tracks faced real hazards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Merrow's towns once set clocks by the sun. Railway schedules made this confusing and unsafe, so the company used one standard time, which spread despite objections and later became law.$q$, $q$The summary ending "spread despite objections and later became law" gives the full sequence from sun time to law without judging it. The summary calling sun time "wiser" adds the opinion that sun time was "wiser" and that residents "lost something valuable," which the passage does not state.$q$, 'draft', '1bd1fd44-46a0-568c-8fbe-05daf0e93544')
