  ('b6646746-d0aa-511d-ab12-899d990420c2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-main-idea-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which detail best supports the claim that better chairs changed how the sport was played?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Early players could push forward well enough in their heavy everyday chairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Lighter, more stable chairs allowed faster breaks, tighter defense and plays that were once impossible.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The builders replaced the steel frame of Okafor's chair with lighter tubing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Today's sports chairs are often fitted to each athlete's body like running shoes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lighter, more stable chairs allowed faster breaks, tighter defense and plays that were once impossible.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 directly describes changes in play caused by the new chairs. The lighter tubing is a design change, a cause, not evidence of how the game itself changed.$q$, 'draft', '466576c1-bad1-576d-8384-9b3c0b9d2894')
