  ('0a0ccace-72d7-536f-ac77-4f9f460c10d3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-main-idea-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs until manufacturers designed new ones on their own and then taught players how to use them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs. Athletes worked with builders to create lighter chairs with lower seats and angled wheels, which made play faster and changed the sport's strategies.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Angling the tops of a chair's wheels inward, called camber, widens its base at the floor. This makes the chair harder to tip and allows tighter turns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs, which was unfair to athletes. Thanks to heroic players like Okafor, the sport finally became worth watching for fans everywhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Early wheelchair basketball used heavy hospital chairs. Athletes worked with builders to create lighter chairs with lower seats and angled wheels, which made play faster and changed the sport's strategies.$q$, $q$The summary that says athletes worked with builders covers the starting point, the cooperative changes and their effect on the game. The summary saying manufacturers designed new chairs "on their own" reverses the passage, which says change "came largely from the athletes themselves."$q$, 'draft', '466576c1-bad1-576d-8384-9b3c0b9d2894')
